[engl]
{100}{}{Tycho}
{200}{}{You see Tycho.}
{210}{}{You see a man in dusty leather armor with a trenchcoat and gas mask.}
{1000}{}{[AUTO-GENERATED SKELETON: replace this entry with the NPC's initial greeting and
conditions.]}
{1010}{}{[MANUAL: initial branch condition/greeting -> Tycho28]}
{2000}{}{Yes?}
{2010}{}{Nothing. Never mind.}
{2020}{}{Duh-wah?}
{2030}{}{I think maybe we should stick together, after all.}
{3000}{}{What can I do for you?}
{3010}{}{Uh, never mind.}
{3020}{}{Any recommendations?}
{3030}{}{Any recommendations?}
{3040}{}{Any recommendations?}
{3050}{}{Any recommendations?}
{3060}{}{Any recommendations?}
{3070}{}{Any recommendations?}
{3080}{}{Thanks for your help. I think it's time to part ways.}
{3090}{}{I need to change formation.}
{3100}{}{What sorts of weapon skills have you learned?}
{4000}{}{Yeah, I'd stay the hell away from whatever made that. Seriously, I've never seen
anything like that. I think our best option is to move on, fast.}
{4010}{}{[Done.]}
{5000}{}{Watch out for radioactive hot spots. This place obviously sustained a direct nuclear
strike, and secondary cascade radiation may be bad. I'd recommend avoiding this place
completely if we can.}
{5010}{}{[Done.]}
{6000}{}{Note the lack of any animal life for quite a distance. And the piles of bones. Whatever
lives here is a real beast. Keep your weapon handy.}
{6010}{}{[Done.]}
{7000}{}{There are many strange tales about Necropolis, the city of the dead. Stay alert, because
it could get dangerous really fast.}
{7010}{}{[Done.]}
{8000}{}{I bet we could get through those force-field generators with a little hot-wiring, or if
we could find the force field control computer.}
{8010}{}{[Done.]}
{9000}{}{A military place like this must have a central command room somewhere.}
{9010}{}{[Done.]}
{10000}{}{Very well. I must say that it has been an honor and a pleasure.}
{10010}{}{[Done.]}
{11000}{}{What distance do you want me at?}
{11010}{}{Stay close.}
{11020}{}{Keep a moderate distance.}
{11030}{}{Move out to longer range.}
{12000}{}{Pretty good ranger training: I can use a spear, of course, in a pinch; I'm also skilled
with small pistols and rifles.}
{12010}{}{[Done.]}
{13000}{}{Another new face. Travelers here are a dime a dozen. But you have the look of someone
different. Care to join me for a drink?}
{13010}{}{Sorry, I'm rather pressed for time.}
{13020}{}{Sure.}
{13030}{}{Duh-wah?}
{14000}{}{Delightful. I hope you don't mind your drink well-watered - they treat beer here like
it's a potted plant.}
{14010}{}{So, what's your story?}
{15000}{}{I could ask the same of you. In the interest of amity, I suppose I'll tell first. I'm
called Tycho. Came from out east, what used to be called Nevada.}
{15010}{}{That's a pretty long trip.}
{15020}{}{How did you survive all the dangers?}
{16000}{}{Yeah, it was. Decided to take it easy for a while. This place shows some promise, just
as soon as someone cleans up some of the scum.}
{16010}{}{Why don't you?}
{16020}{}{Yeah, I noticed. What do you know about those jerks?}
{17000}{}{Not my place. I'd rather not cross Killian, after all. He'll clean up this town when he
gets around to it. A good man, mark my words. But watch out for that fellow Gizmo.
Reminds me of another fat freak my father told me about back in Las Vegas.}
{17010}{}{Thanks for the tip, and the drink.}
{18000}{}{Whoa, not so fast. We never finished introductions, remember? What's your name,
stranger?
---
I'm
---
.}
{18010}{}{None of your business, you nut.}
{19000}{}{Now, now, no need to get impolite. But with that attitude you'd best be on your way.}
{19010}{}{Whatever. See ya.}
{19020}{}{Bite me.}
{20000}{}{There's two grades of scum here. One of 'em's the Skulz, a gang that hangs out in back
of Marcelles' crash house. They're just grade-B twerps. But the other ones answer to a
fat freak whose name you can probably guess. Runs the casino. Those guys are organized
and dangerous.}
{20010}{}{I see. Thanks for the info.}
{20020}{}{[MANUAL: add player response/transition -> Goodbyes]}
{21000}{}{Had some pretty good training, and some good weapons, too. My grandfather was a Ranger
way back when, and he taught my father everything he knew. Dad passed it on to me. So I
know enough not to drink glowing water, so to speak.}
{21010}{}{Interesting. Thanks for the drink.}
{21020}{}{Really? Survival's tough these days. You must be pretty knowledgeable.}
{22000}{}{Yeah, well, my family taught me everything there is to know about survival. Don't drink
water that's totally clear and free of insects and moss, for instance. Only poisonous or
radioactive water would be that clean in the wilderness. Lots of other little things to
look out for, too.}
{22010}{}{Interesting. Thanks for the drink.}
{22020}{}{Like what?}
{23000}{}{Well, if you've got some time, I could go over some pointers.}
{23010}{}{Sorry, I'm kind of pressed for time.}
{23020}{}{Sure, that would be great.}
{24000}{}{I hope that my little instruction course helped a bit.}
{24010}{}{[MANUAL: add player response/transition -> Goodbyes]}
{25000}{}{Yeah, a drink of water. Never mind.}
{25010}{}{[Done.]}
{26000}{}{Word out is that you've been having some contacts with Gizmo. I'd step carefully around
that barrel of lard if I were you.}
{26010}{}{Duh-wah?}
{26020}{}{My business is none of yours.}
{26030}{}{Yeah, I work for Gizmo now. What's it to you?}
{27000}{}{Fair enough. But watch your back. Gizmo isn't known for his consideration for his
employees.}
{27010}{}{[Done.]}
{28000}{}{Suffice to say that your employer has caused more than enough misery and strife in this
town. Don't expect much help from anyone, least of all Gizmo. Too bad. You might've been
able to change this town for the better.}
{28010}{}{[Done.]}
{29000}{}{What do you want?}
{29010}{}{I need information about the gangers here.}
{29020}{}{Sorry to disturb your private time. Go wank somewhere else.}
{29030}{}{I need information about the town.}
{30000}{}{Well, this is the Skum Pitt, a wretched hive of villainy and all that. Just west of here
is Gizmo's, a big casino. Word is the games are rigged. A little south of here is the
Crash House, run by Marcelles, where you can get a night's sleep for way too many caps.
Past that is Killian's. Killian runs a general store, and he also enforces the law in
this town - a good man. Then south of there you have Doc Morbid, whose operation is a
little funny, if you take my meaning.}
{30010}{}{[MANUAL: add player response/transition -> Goodbyes]}
{31000}{}{Hello again. How can I help you?}
{31010}{}{I need information about the gangers here.}
{31020}{}{I need information about the town.}
{31030}{}{Killian's asked me to clean up this town, and I'd like your help.}
{32000}{}{Well it's about time. Lead on, my friend, and let's do some street sweeping. I'd
recommend knocking over Gizmo, if I may.
---
Well it's about time. Lead on, my friend, and let's do some street sweeping. I'd
recommend knocking over Gizmo, if I may.}
{32010}{}{[MANUAL: add player response/transition -> TychoJoins]}

